        {
          "file": "tests/frontier-baseline-graphics.test.mjs",
          "tests": 16,
          "passed": 16,
          "topLevel": [
            "a window that draws and idles at the refresh period is a measurement",
            "the idle reference is the median of the half-sums of consecutive pairs",
            "a presented window at 120 Hz whose idle median falls in the low group is a measurement (attempt A8 of the baseline)",
            "a window that draws but that no display paces is rejected as unpaced",
            "a single large stall in a loop that nothing paces does not make it paced",
            "the threshold is half of the refresh period that the window read back",
            "a presented window at 60 Hz is a measurement, whichever way its intervals fall",
            "a window that does not draw is rejected as undrawn, whatever its pace",
            "the statistics across runs refuse an unpaced run, and say which value failed",
            "the frames above twice the idle reference do not depend on the group the median falls in",
            "a receipt with an unpaced accepted run is refused",
            "a receipt written under the idle reference accepts a run whose median is in the low group",
            "a receipt recorded before the idle reference is judged by the median it was judged by, and still verifies",
            "a count above twice the idle reference that is not a count of the samples is refused",
            "a lane that was not presented reports no frame-time statistic, and keeps what it rejected",
            "a lane that claims to be presented has all its runs and their statistics"
          ]
        },
        {
          "file": "tests/frontier-comparison-protocol.test.mjs",
          "tests": 17,
          "passed": 17,
          "topLevel": [
            "the protocol has every required field with its type, and the validator is not vacuous",
            "the three arms, the three hypotheses and the four windows are the ones decided",
            "the secondary outcomes are the ones decided, and each axis with a verdict carries its margin",
            "only the thresholds can be frozen, each with a rule and a source, and both fields move together",
            "the pin: the protocol without its freeze fields has the SHA-256 recorded here",
            "an amendment says what changed, why, the text it replaces and that no comparative measurement came before it",
            "a change of the protocol after the pre-registration fails unless it comes with an amendment and a pin",
            "while the comparative executions have not run, an amendment cannot count measurements before it",
            "the categories are exactly gain, neutral, cost and inconclusive, and exclusive and exhaustive for any interval",
            "the margin is the larger of 10% of B's median and 0.5 ms, and the examples land where the research note says",
            "a gain is always better: the interval of an outcome where higher is better is negated, and a gain in FPS excludes zero",
            "Holm over the four windows of H3 stands for the smallest p-values in order and only ever downgrades",
            "the order of the executions is a Latin square repeated, balanced in count and position",
            "the load limit is written and the redo of an execution is bounded",
            "the percentiles, the median, the interquartile range and the bootstrap are defined and reproducible",
            "the research note covers the protocol it reads and quotes its pin and its examples",
            "this test is part of the contracts"
          ]
        },
        {
          "file": "tests/frontier-baseline-heap.test.mjs",
          "tests": 10,
          "passed": 10,
          "topLevel": [
            "the hosted series are 32 readings that move in a band wider than the limit, with no trend",
            "the hosted series pass with a growth of 0: the median of the last half is the median of the first",
            "the floors judged the hosted run wrongly: five-round floors failed process 2 by 8 bytes, the floors of the halves are 320 apart in both",
